 README.md  | 13 +++++++++++++
 Staticfile |  1 +
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 Staticfile

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 9e774b5..0cc5f25 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -746,6 +746,19 @@ Then hit the **Deploy site** button and your **Portfolio Site** is live 🥳
 
 <br>
 
+### Deploy to Wasmer
+
+[![Deploy to Wasmer](https://img.shields.io/badge/Deploy%20to-Wasmer-171717?logo=wasmer&logoColor=white)](https://wasmer.io/apps/create?github=rammcodes%2FDopefolio)
+
+You can also host your portfolio on [Wasmer Edge](https://docs.wasmer.io/edge/):
+
+1. Fork Dopefolio (or push your clone) to your own GitHub account and make your changes there. The button above imports this original repository; it does not create a copy in your account. To deploy your own portfolio, import your own repository on the Wasmer import page.
+2. Commit the compiled `css/style.css` whenever you change the SASS files (`npm run compile:scss`). The `Staticfile` in the repository root (`root: .`) tells Wasmer to serve the committed files as they are, without running `npm install` or a build (Wasmer's builder reads this file; it does not change how you work on the site locally). If the import page shows a different preset, select the static site (staticfile) preset.
+
+**Note:** the contact form's `action="#"` is not configured, so form submissions go nowhere until you set it up (for example with **formspree.io**, as described in the Contact Section above). The Google Fonts stylesheet loads from fonts.googleapis.com.
+
+<br>
+
 ---
 
 <br>
diff --git a/Staticfile b/Staticfile
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..fdbb02c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Staticfile
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+root: .
